	<div id="main"><h1>Governor's Executive Orders 2009</h1>
<div id="navcontainer">
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_001">Executive Order 09-01</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon establishes the Missouri Automotive Jobs Task Force. (Jan. 13)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_002">Executive Order 09-02</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon establishes the Governor’s Economic Stimulus Coordination Council. (Jan. 13)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_003">Executive Order 09-03</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon directs the Missouri Department of Economic Development, working with the Missouri Development Finance Board, to create a pool of funds designated for low-interest and no-interest direct loans for small businesses. (Jan. 13)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_004">Executive Order 09-04</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon declares a State of Emergency and directs the Missouri State Emergency Operations Plan be activated in response to severe storms that started on January 26, 2009. (Jan. 26)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_005">Executive Order 09-05</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon establishes the Complete Count Committee to ensure that Missouri has an accurate count of its citizens during the 2010 United States Census of Population. This Executive Order supersedes and replaces <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2008/eo08_034">Executive Order 08-34</a>. (Jan. 27)<br>- Superseded and Replaced by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2018/eo12">Executive Order 18-12</a><br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_006">Executive Order 09-06</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders and directs the Adjutant General to call into active service any state militia deemed necessary to support civilian authorities in response to the aftermath of severe weather that began on January 26, 2009. (Jan. 28)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_007">Executive Order 09-07</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders the Acting Director of the Department of Natural Resources vested with full discretionary authority to temporarily waive or suspend statutory or administrative rule or regulation to serve the interests of public health and safety during the period of emergency and subsequent recovery period in response to severe weather that began on January 26, 2009. (Jan. 30)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_008">Executive Order 09-08</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon designates members of his staff to have supervisory authority over departments, divisions, and agencies of state government. (Feb. 2)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_009">Executive Order 09-09</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders the transfer of various scholarship programs under the Departments of Agriculture, Elementary and Secondary Education, Higher Education, and Natural Resources to the Department of Higher Education. (Feb. 4)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_010">Executive Order 09-10</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders the Department of Elementary and Secondary Education and the Department of Economic Development to transfer the Missouri Customized Training Program to the Department of Economic Development. (Feb. 4)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_011">Executive Order 09-11</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders the Department of Health and Senior Services and the Department of Social Services to transfer the Blindness Education, Screening and Treatment (BEST) Program to the Department of Social Services. (Feb.4)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_012">Executive Order 09-12</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon establishes the Transform Missouri Initiative to analyze the American Recovery and Reinvestment Act of 2009 to benefit state programs and projects. (Feb. 20)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_017">Executive Order 09-17</a><br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_013">Executive Order 09-13</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon extends the declaration of emergency contained in <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_004">Executive Order 09-04</a> and the terms of <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_007">Executive Order 09-07</a> through March 31, 2009, for the purpose of continuing the cleanup efforts in affected communities. (Feb. 25)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_014">Executive Order 09-14</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon designates members of his staff to have supervisory authority over departments, divisions, and agencies of state government. (Mar. 5)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_015">Executive Order 09-15</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon expands the Missouri Automotive Jobs Task Force membership, created by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_001">Executive Order 09-01</a>, to consist of 18 members. (Mar. 24)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_016">Executive Order 09-16</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon directs the Department of Corrections to lead a permanent, interagency steering team for the Missouri Reentry Process (MRP) to integrate offender reentry practices in state agencies and communities. (Mar. 26)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_017">Executive Order 09-17</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon creates the Transform Missouri Project as well as the Taxpayer Accountability, Compliance and Transparency Unit. Personnel assigned to the Transform Missouri Initiative established by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_012">Executive Order 09-12</a> are transferred to the Transform Missouri Project and <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_012">Executive Order 09-12</a> is rescinded. (Mar. 31)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_018">Executive Order 09-18</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders all state agencies with building management under the Office of Administration to institute policies of energy efficiency as a priority. The Office of Administration will develop a State Building Energy Efficiency Design Standard with standards to be adopted by all state agencies. (Apr. 23)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_019">Executive Order 09-19</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon declares a State of Emergency and directs the Missouri State Emergency Operations Plan be activated in response to severe weather that began on May 8, 2009. (May 8)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_020">Executive Order 09-20</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders the Director of the Department of Natural Resources vested with full discretionary authority to temporarily waive or suspend statutory or administrative rule or regulation to serve the interests of public health and safety during the period of emergency and subsequent recovery period in response to severe weather that began on May 8, 2009. (May 12)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_021">Executive Order 09-21</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon declares a State of Emergency and directs the Missouri State Emergency Operations Plan to remain activated due to severe weather that began on May 8, 2009. (May 14)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_022">Executive Order 09-22</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon appoints the Home Building and Residential Energy Efficiency Advisory Panel to issue recommendations on energy efficiency measures for the home building sector and consumers. (Aug. 20)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_023">Executive Order 09-23</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon designates members of his staff to have supervisory authority over departments, divisions, and agencies of state government. (Sep. 1)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_024">Executive Order 09-24</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon creates the Prompt Pay for a Healthy Missouri Project to examine issues on timely reimbursement of Missouri hospitals and health care providers by health insurance companies. (Sep. 11)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_025">Executive Order 09-25</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon establishes the Governor's Faith-Based and Community Service Partnership for Disaster Recovery to improve the use of public and private sector resources for emergency human service functions in natural disasters and terrorist events. (Sep. 21)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_026">Executive Order 09-26</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders state offices to be closed on Friday, November 27, 2009. (Oct. 30)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_027">Executive Order 09-27</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon creates the Missouri Office of Health Information Technology, referred to as MO-HITECH to promote the development and application of an effective healthcare information exchange infrastructure. <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2006/eo06_003">Executive Order 06-03</a> is rescinded. (Nov. 4)<br>-Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_028">Executive Order 09-28</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon establishes the post of Missouri Poet Laureate. This Executive Order supersedes and replaces <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2008/eo08_001">Executive Order 08-01</a>. (Dec. 24)<br>- Superseded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2016/eo6">Executive Order 16-06</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2009/eo09_029">Executive Order 09-29</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon outlines the suspension of federal commercial motor vehicle and driver laws during emergency declarations. This Executive Order will supersede Executive Orders <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2007/eo07_001">07-01</a> and <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2008/eo08_040">08-40</a> on February 1, 2010. (Dec. 31)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
</div>
<p>
